+/*
+ * End an entry and leave the read stream where the next header begins.
+ *
+ * The sliding window reads ahead, so when an entry is done -- extracted or
+ * skipped -- some of its ciphertext is usually still sitting unread in the
+ * stream. bytes_remaining cannot be used to skip it, because that counts
+ * decrypted bytes still owed to the consumer, and the two have drifted apart by
+ * whatever the window buffered. enc_remaining is the authoritative count of
+ * what is genuinely left.
